---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
What moving the project to another series takes, addon by addon: available, an open migration pull request to review, or to migrate (dependencies first); own addons apart.

In a plain clone of an addons repository (no `[tool.odx]` project), the addons of the repository instead: those on `<remote>/<from>` and not yet on `<remote>/<to>`.

Usage: odx migrate plan [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --to <SERIES>
          Target series [default: `[tool.odx.upgrade] target_odoo_version`; mandatory outside a project]

      --from <SERIES>
          Outside a project: the source series [default: the series before --to]

      --remote <NAME>
          Outside a project: the remote both series come from [default: `upstream` when it exists, else `origin`]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml to use (a repos.yaml for the commands that read one)

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve git repositories and forge and index data from the cache only; what is not cached fails. Local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Say when each repository's fetch and build starts, and what each fetched and merged

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on standard error: no progress lines, no warnings
